  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Area-based Support to Strengthen Resilience in Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to accompany communities from crisis to recovery, building on experience and lessons learned by both Enabling Community Recovery and Resilience (ENCORE) and Rakhine Triple Nexus (RTN). The project will be implemented through ENCORE and RTN , and cover Rakhine State, Kachin State, Shan State, Mon State, Kayin State, Bago Region, Mandalay Region, Thanintharyi Region and Magway Region.The project has been designed to include a multi-layered and cross-sectoral intervention that aims to strengthen the capacity of individuals, households, community and civil society groups to prepare, respond and cope with future stresses, but also quickly reduce the caseload of humanitarian agencies, preventing inter-generational poverty and significantly reducing the number and the impact of future humanitarian crises. The project aims to strengthen and empower civil society, community structures, women and youth groups to amplify the voices of vulnerable communities and promote social cohesion and inclusive development.</narrative>
  </description>
